emp/STORY-260830-ptxkqe/worktree verify-commit HEAD` reports a good signature for oparin@me.com, the commit's tree equals the accepted CR candidate tree, its parent is 2fc6d5074058ab7970c87982deac50b3e3f5fd91, `git status` in the Story worktree is clean apart from the board checkout artifact, and `task-board worktree status STORY-260830-ptxkqe` shows the CR checkpointed and the task integrating; (4) attach TASK-260830-1geqhj_checkpoint-rev4.md as a task-scoped outcome with every command, exit code and OID; then exit. Do NOT change the task status, do NOT make product changes, do NOT commit manually, do NOT integrate or land the Story, do NOT run a generic handoff, do NOT rerun product suites (accept the immutable review evidence; claim no executions you did not perform). If the checkpoint command refuses, attach the refusal verbatim in the outcome and exit non-zero without any repair attempt. Model: muse-spark max. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board.\n\n\n\n\n\n## Evidence and Safety\n\n- Add/update a task-scoped outcome named `TASK-260830-1geqhj_*` before handoff:\n  `task-board m 'add_resource(TASK-260830-1geqhj, name=TASK-260830-1geqhj_results.md, content=\"...\", type=outcome, description=\"Handoff evidence\")'`\n- Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior ships with negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject; prove the bound by narrowing it, not only by deleting it, and name the production call site. Shapes and incidents: `references/negative-evidence.md`.\n- An absence and a failure to read are different facts; report unknown instead of inferring a property from a proxy signal.\n- Stop-The-Line only for an evidence-backed external blocker or unresolved human-only product/platform/architecture/approval decision. Persist evidence, failed attempts, options/tradeoffs, recommendation, and exact input needed; otherwise rework autonomously.\n- `integrating` is the role handoff status; use it only after the evidence contract is satisfied.\n\n## LAST — Run For Role Handoff\n\nAfter AC, checklist, validation, and outcome evidence:\n\n```bash\ntask-board handoff TASK-260830-1geqhj --role developer\n```\n\n## Working Directory\nBoard directory: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board`\n\nWork in the project root. Never edit board files directly.\n\n## Story Workspace\n\nYou are running in an isolated Git worktree for STORY-260830-ptxkqe.\n\n- Workspace path: `.temp/STORY-260830-ptxkqe/worktree` (this is your working directory)\n- Branch: `task-board/story/STORY-260830-ptxkqe`, forked from `main`\n- Authoritative board: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board` (already exported as `TASK_BOARD_DIR`)\n\nMake every repository change here. Do not commit, switch, rebase, merge, or delete this branch, and do not run `task-board` against the `.task-board` copy inside this worktree — it is a checkout artifact, not the board. Integration into trunk is the orchestrator's step, not yours.\n\nLeave your work UNCOMMITTED in the worktree — the handoff snapshots the working tree against the recorded checkpoint. A commit of your own on this branch is refused at handoff with `change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint`, and the repair is `git reset --soft <checkpoint_oid>` before completing again.\n\n## Integration Assignment\n\nThis is the integration run for accepted Change Request `CR-TASK-260830-1geqhj-4` revision 4. The immutable producer binding is role `developer` (archetype `implementer`). Keep the board at `integrating`; only the integration transaction may write `done`. This assignment supersedes generic producer FIRST/LAST status and handoff instructions: run the bound checkpoint or integration command, attach fresh task-scoped outcome evidence, then end without calling the generic `handoff` command or setting status yourself.\n"}}
