{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4bb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b1e8-6498-7322-b5d6-d665ebf7eabc"},"sequence":184,"recorded_at":1780531400000363,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5c20913d-2f3d-47fb-bfa3-cadda84f302f","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"5c20913d-2f3d-47fb-bfa3-cadda84f302f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5c20913d-2f3d-47fb-bfa3-cadda84f302f"},"call_id":"call_01a0b1e8ecf876beb7fd0237e9a03301","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-8-1\",\n  \"command\": \"export TASK_BOARD_DIR=/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board\\n/Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board q 'get(TASK-260830-1geqhj) { status checklist }' 2>&1 | head -30\",\n  \"description\": \"Read task status and checklist\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"{\\\"checklist\\\":[{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Production entry points implement the scoped deliverable: Implement ax pane SESSION_ID validation of owner epoch, fencing, materialization, profile, provider identity, and resume authorization\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Relevant positive, negative, compatibility, and recovery tests pass with logs attached\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"README/doctor/capability evidence and specification traceability are updated without unsupported claims\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Code written per task description and AC\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"In a managed Story worktree the candidate is left UNCOMMITTED in the worktree for the handoff to snapshot — never commit on the Story branch. A producer commit moves the branch tip off the recorded checkpoint and the handoff refuses with change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint; repair with `git reset --soft \\\\u003ccheckpoint_oid\\\\u003e` before completing again.\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio — `n of m AC rows driven` — and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant — the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"A gate that inspects source text is additionally attacked by a mutant that PRESERVES the searched-for token and changes behavior, and the mutant harness executes the behavioral suite, not only the static checker.\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Lint clean\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Implementation matches AC\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Solution fits project architecture\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Tests green\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"Gate, refusal, validation, authorization, and attestation behavior attacked, not read — positive-path-only evidence is not accepted\\\",\\\"done\\\":true},{\\\"text\\\":\\\"If review does not accept the work — verdict evidence added and status routed by the explicit verdict branches\\\",\\\"done\\\":true}],\\\"status\\\":\\\"integrating\\\"}\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 2936,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 734,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4bd","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b1e8-6498-7322-b5d6-d665ebf7eabc"},"sequence":185,"recorded_at":1780531400000365,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5c20913d-2f3d-47fb-bfa3-cadda84f302f","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"5c20913d-2f3d-47fb-bfa3-cadda84f302f","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5c20913d-2f3d-47fb-bfa3-cadda84f302f"},"call_id":"call_01a0b1e8f29976d7a843ae178649b12f","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-1geqhj/TASK-260830-1geqhj_reviewer-cr4.md`.\n1|Independently review Change Request revision 4 of TASK-260830-1geqhj (implement-ax-pane-enforcement-wrapper, first leaf of STORY-260830-ptxkqe ax-pane-and-terminal-instance-binding; siblings 2056mm and kkh1an follow; task_delta on the Story branch (trunk base 2fc6d5074058ab7970c87982deac50b3e3f5fd91; checkpointed predecessors none; tip 2fc6d5074058ab7970c87982deac50b3e3f5fd91), published by RUN-260917-ca6552 on muse-spark max, 24 changed paths, patch and validation log attached as TASK-260830-1geqhj_change-request_rev4.patch / _rev4-validation.log. Revisions 1..3 are earlier construction attempts of the same producer scope that failed the Change Request validation suite on the pre-PR51 10m race-test timeout under concurrent suites; they carry no review verdict and no prior review findings — review revision 4 on its own merits.). Read the producer brief TASK-260830-1geqhj_producer.md, the outcome TASK-260830-1geqhj_results.md, TASK-260830-1geqhj_conformance-matrix.md, TASK-260830-1geqhj_producer-evidence.tar.gz (validation logs, sessquery-rerun.log, sessquery-long.log, mutant logs), internal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md in the candidate, the CR patch and validation log, and the exact immutable CR bytes. The normative authority is the pinned internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md Sections 4.B, 4.C (the wrapper rule and the after-restore sequence 1-5, the tmux/-S server and background-caller rules, the sentinel/managername rule), 4.D, 5.2 Terminal Events, 7.A and 13.1 steps 3-4.\n2|\n3|Verify with your own instruments. (0) REWORK VERIFICATION FIRST — revision 3 was routed CHANGES REQUESTED by RUN-260917-19551c, which graded every other rev2 finding FIXED on its own executed evidence (the epoch-1 owner restores and reattaches, supersession keeps every pair's receipt through real-SIGKILL seams, the no-checkpoint-store guard is right, the losing-epoch Emit arm and create-from-stopped are pinned, the foreground credential path and the realm-order dependence are closed) and blocked on ONE class at two sites: the strict `Winner.Checkpoint == NewestCheckpointID` agreement parks the ordinary POST-TAKEOVER lifecycle (a successor lease's checkpoint is the handoff base and never moves, so agreement holds only until the new owner's first checkpoint — every taken-over session could then never restore on its own owner), while `Run` still derived the profile closure from `Winner.Checkpoint`, which on the exact tree produced a `yolo` launch with `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox` on a session whose authoritative profile is `standard`. The reviewer also proved that relaxing the agreement ALONE converts the park into exactly that wrong-profile launch, so the two must land together. Plus P2-1 (a post-window same-pair race through `Run` reports `launch` carrying the WINNER's child) and eight P3. Read TASK-260830-1geqhj_review-verdict-rev3.md and TASK-260830-1geqhj_review-evidence-rev3.tar.gz, re-run their probes against the NEW tree, and grade each finding. Check specifically: the fold is now the SOLE newest-checkpoint authority and the only lease-derived assertion is the implication 'a checkpoint-carrying winner implies a published newest', at one site every launch-class path passes; nothing else about the lease base is asserted; the profile closure comes from the checkpoint actually RESUMED (required checkpoint, else the fold's newest loaded through sessckpt, else the session head) and a mutant that reads `Winner.Checkpoint` again dies; the wrong-profile plants exist in BOTH directions through `Run`; the post-window same-pair race now reattaches; and the coverage ratio was re-derived on the fixed tree (43 rows; the previous producer published 43/43 while the reviewer measured 39/43). Then proceed to your own independent review of the whole revision: (1) Spec fidelity — extract the after-restore sequence and the wrapper preconditions from the pinned text yourself and diff them against Decide/Run: the order (latest local lease -> bounded mesh refresh -> resume only with the winning lease AND valid required materialization -> offer remote attach/takeover interactively -> otherwise parked without launching), the park reason vocabulary (remote_owner|stale_owner|restore_policy|failed_handoff), the background-caller rule (capability_unavailable with typed realm/readiness details, never direct server creation), the \"cached sentinel or prior managername observation MUST NOT authorize resume\" rule (confirm it is structural, not a comment: plant a cached-sentinel input that would authorize and check the refusal), the idempotency contract on (session_id, bootstrap_operation_id) with idempotency_mismatch for a changed operation in the bootstrap window and \"status plus that binding MUST prove absence or identify the one child\" after a lost result, and \"never persists or replicates a PID\" (grep the package and the receipt shape). (2) Composition, not re-implementation — every check must call the landed gate: fencing.AuthorizeActivation/AuthorizeRestore for epoch/fencing, matjournal/sessckpt for materialization and checkpoint admission, sessprofile.Derive + provhost.ResolveMapping for profile and profile_mapping_unavailable, provhost/resumesmoke for identity/tuple/smoke preconditions, terminalbackend for backend identity and closed capabilities, axerror for every class; plant a bypass for each (call the decision core with a state the gate would refuse but the wrapper might accept on its own) and confirm the composition catches it; confirm no gate logic was copied (diff the decision core against the gate packages for duplicated predicates). (3) Decision table — drive Decide with the full matrix of inputs and assert exactly one outcome per row (41 claimed): lower/losing/future/foreign/expired/malformed/absent/ambiguous/unverified/failed-handoff/remote ownership, invalid or uncommitted materialization, unattested or mismatched checkpoint, unmapped profile, unresolved identity/realm, backend probe mismatch, background caller without an attested server, changed bootstrap operation, lost-result reattach; add at least six plants of your own (two conflicting arms both satisfiable; an interactive remote owner that should offer takeover but with an expired grant; a winning lease with a materialization one generation behind; a profile source event that is not authoritative; a descriptor whose backend generation differs; a capability row not in the closed set) and report admitted/refused/parked with the exact class. (4) Durable bootstrap — no-replace + fsync + hooks: rerun the real-kill crash test twice; inject your own crash between binding write and receipt and after the receipt, and confirm restart proves absence or identifies the one child, never a second child; confirm identical retries reattach without a second write (inode/mtime census). (5) Events — §5.2 authoring goes through sessrepo.AppendEvent under the current lease with the exact payload shapes (session.parked with its reason, terminal.created, session.resumed v4 members): plant an append under a losing lease and confirm refusal. (6) Mutation — rerun the shipped harness in an isolated copy, rerun each KILLED twice, plant at least four narrowing mutants of your own on composition arms the producer did not mutate (one gate result ignored; the after-restore order swapped at steps 3/4; the park reason collapsed to one value; the bootstrap window check dropped) plus an applied harmless SURVIVED control; per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits, precise denominators. (7) The red race gate — the producer reports internal/sessquery hitting the default 10m race timeout (37/38 packages ok; isolated rerun exit 0 in 552s with -timeout 20m) and does not claim it as a pass: judge it (import census showing axpane cannot reach sessquery; the 96s figure measured on an idle machine during the STORY-260830-1oqfec landing) and rerun it yourself while nothing else runs; say plainly whether the gate is a host-capacity artifact or a real regression. (8) Bounds and hygiene — no ax CLI, no tmux/ConPTY process control, no provider process (the stated bound); internal/traceability untouched (final leaf owns it); README package section with test commands and no capability claim; changed_paths exactly the candidate paths, no __pycache__/.pyc; gofmt/vet clean; go test ./internal/axpane ./internal/fencing ./internal/sessprofile ./internal/matjournal ./internal/sessckpt ./internal/provhost -count=1 green; tracecheck and `cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` exit 0 on the exact tree.\n4|\n5|Method: isolated immutable probes only, never mutate the live Story worktree, index, branch or HEAD; no product edits, commits, checkpoints or integration; Curator go-testing-tools skill; all CI local; PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 for every harness; keep scratch small under .temp/TASK-260830-1geqhj/ and delete candidate copies when done. Attach TASK-260830-1geqhj_review-verdict-rev4.md and TASK-260830-1geqhj_review-evidence-rev4.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), complete the live merged checklist, then accept_cr(TASK-260830-1geqhj, revision=4, evidence=TASK-260830-1geqhj_review-verdict-rev4.md) or hand off changes requested with P1/P2/P3 classes named. Model: claude-opus-5 max. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
